{
  "abstract": "We audit a conditional Route B representation of the leading-order nonabelian overlap integrals in Modal Triplet Theory using the self-dual Yang-Mills twistor corner. A standard twistor action is holomorphic BF-type; it does not by itself provide the positive Hermitian norm or relative coupling normalization used by Route A. We isolate a reconstruction-and-norm bridge as an explicit assumption. The SU(2) comparison also assumes that the directional curvature is twice the Fubini-Study form and uses the effective round-sphere lens model. The SU(3) comparison uses the declared auxiliary nilmanifold, color harmonic, and factorization assumption of Paper II. Under these shared inputs, Route B reproduces the SU(2) overlap as four pi times the squared lens amplitude-radius product, and the SU(3) overlap as the integrated squared color-harmonic norm. The result is a conditional dictionary check, not an independent selection of overlap values or a completed nonabelian Theta-closure theorem.",
